  "decision": "Retain and default only the gfx1151 serial-c1 Q5T16 K6144/N5120 tile8 owner. It is BF16-bit exact, wins both 512 process orders plus 1K/4K, improves every natural AR scope, adds no bytes, and leaves native rows/MTP and all policy misses on the registered direct fallback. This is development evidence, not a clean publication topline; P5 remains open because Vulkan AR is still faster."
